From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: a click on a Wine window behind a Linux one brings it forward

0700 deactivates Wine's active window when a Linux program's window takes
the front, so that a Wine window coming forward again is noticed and the
desktop raised (XDESKTOP). That happened only when the compositor's list
showed the change; a Linux window brought forward by its own taskbar button
set the state directly and skipped it. The Wine window stayed Wine's active
one, a click on it was no news, and the Linux window stayed on top (David
2026-10-01: Linux programs always on top). The button now deactivates it
too.
---
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -2656,8 +2656,18 @@
         sg_xwin_command( win, away ? L"XMINIMIZE" : L"XACTIVATE" );
         if (!away)
         {
+            HWND fg = GetForegroundWindow();
+
             sg_xwin_front = TRUE;
             sg_xwin_front_time = GetTickCount();
+            /* Wine's active window is behind it now: deactivated, as when a
+             * click puts a Linux window in front, so a click on that Wine
+             * window brings it forward again (it stayed Wine's active
+             * window, the click was no news, and the Linux window stayed on
+             * top -- David 2026-10-01) */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_XWIN_BUTTON_KEEPS_ACTIVE
+            if (fg && fg != tray_window && fg != GetDesktopWindow()) SetForegroundWindow( GetDesktopWindow() );
+#endif
         }
         sg_sync_xwindows();
         return;
